        <h2>Patient-specific medical engineering</h2>

        <p>
            At Zimmer Biomet, I worked in the Patient Specific Instruments (PSI)
            team, supporting the development of customized surgical solutions
            based on patient medical imaging data.
        </p>

        <p>
            My main responsibilities involved transforming medical imaging
            information into accurate 3D models and patient-specific surgical
            guides, following established engineering workflows and validation
            procedures.
        </p>

        <h2>Main responsibilities</h2>

        <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>
                <strong>3D CAD Design:</strong>
                Creation and modification of patient-specific anatomical models,
                surgical guides, and implants using specialized CAD workflows.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Medical Imaging:</strong>
                Processing and reconstruction of CT data to support accurate
                anatomical representation and surgical planning.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Digital Surgical Planning:</strong>
                Support for landmark identification, model validation, and
                planning workflows using specialized engineering software.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Process Standardization:</strong>
                Preparation of technical documentation and support for workflow
                improvements and consistency.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Technical Training:</strong>
                Onboarding and guidance for new engineering team members,
                sharing technical knowledge and workflow procedures.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            This experience strengthened my skills in precision engineering,
            3D modelling, medical imaging, technical validation, and
            multidisciplinary collaboration.
        </p>
